\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.9}{\ignorespaces All 14 macro metrics for the principal variants: point estimate [95\% patient-bootstrap percentile interval]. Within each of seeds 44,2026,3407, five fold probabilities are averaged per patient, metrics are computed and averaged over T0--T2, then seed metrics are equally averaged. Threshold-dependent metrics use 0.5. Identical patient resamples preserve pairing across models and landmarks. Entries are marginal model intervals; paired differences are reported separately. Intervals condition on the fitted ensembles and exclude retraining and retrospective selection uncertainty. Downward arrows identify metrics for which lower is better.}}{21}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extended_macro}{{A.9}{21}{All 14 macro metrics for the principal variants: point estimate [95\% patient-bootstrap percentile interval]. Within each of seeds 44,2026,3407, five fold probabilities are averaged per patient, metrics are computed and averaged over T0--T2, then seed metrics are equally averaged. Threshold-dependent metrics use 0.5. Identical patient resamples preserve pairing across models and landmarks. Entries are marginal model intervals; paired differences are reported separately. Intervals condition on the fitted ensembles and exclude retraining and retrospective selection uncertainty. Downward arrows identify metrics for which lower is better}{table.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.10}{\ignorespaces Threshold sensitivity analysis: three-seed mean Macro metrics. Each seed uses landmark-specific Youden thresholds from its disjoint validation-fold scores. OOF single-model scores differ from test fivefold ensemble scores; this is sensitivity analysis, not independent ensemble calibration. No test labels choose thresholds.}}{22}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extended_threshold}{{A.10}{22}{Threshold sensitivity analysis: three-seed mean Macro metrics. Each seed uses landmark-specific Youden thresholds from its disjoint validation-fold scores. OOF single-model scores differ from test fivefold ensemble scores; this is sensitivity analysis, not independent ensemble calibration. No test labels choose thresholds}{table.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.11}{\ignorespaces Exploratory landmark comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled.}}{22}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_landmarks}{{A.11}{22}{Exploratory landmark comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled}{table.11}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.12}{\ignorespaces Exploratory Macro operating and probability-quality comparisons. Differences are first-named minus second-named model; negative Brier, NLL, or ECE differences favor the first model. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled.}}{23}{table.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_extended}{{A.12}{23}{Exploratory Macro operating and probability-quality comparisons. Differences are first-named minus second-named model; negative Brier, NLL, or ECE differences favor the first model. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled}{table.12}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.13}{\ignorespaces Exploratory pooling comparisons: ForecastAttention minus ForecastMean. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled.}}{23}{table.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_pooling}{{A.13}{23}{Exploratory pooling comparisons: ForecastAttention minus ForecastMean. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled}{table.13}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.14}{\ignorespaces Exploratory paired T2 minus T0 comparisons. Shared patient-bootstrap draws retain dependence between seeds and landmarks. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled.}}{24}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_longitudinal}{{A.14}{24}{Exploratory paired T2 minus T0 comparisons. Shared patient-bootstrap draws retain dependence between seeds and landmarks. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across seeds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fixed, retrospectively selected seed44/2026/3407 ensembles; seeds are not resampled}{table.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.7}{\ignorespaces Six complementary landmark summaries: AUROC, AP, F1, sensitivity, specificity, and Brier score. Metrics are computed separately from each seed's five-fold ensemble probabilities and then averaged across seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Error bars show descriptive sample seed standard deviations, while shading gives conditional 95\% shared-patient-bootstrap intervals for the seed mean. The same 175 patients appear at every seed and landmark.}}{24}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:longitudinal}{{A.7}{24}{Six complementary landmark summaries: AUROC, AP, F1, sensitivity, specificity, and Brier score. Metrics are computed separately from each seed's five-fold ensemble probabilities and then averaged across seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Error bars show descriptive sample seed standard deviations, while shading gives conditional 95\% shared-patient-bootstrap intervals for the seed mean. The same 175 patients appear at every seed and landmark}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.8}{\ignorespaces Outcome-conditioned changes in predicted pCR probability from T0 to T2. For each seed-specific five-fold ensemble, every patient contributes one probability change. Histograms summarize these within-seed changes and are then equally averaged across seeds; probabilities are not averaged across seeds before constructing a change distribution. Panels separate models and outcome classes. Repeated seed predictions are correlated observations of the same 175 patients and do not triple the sample size. Score changes do not establish individual treatment effects.}}{25}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scorechanges}{{A.8}{25}{Outcome-conditioned changes in predicted pCR probability from T0 to T2. For each seed-specific five-fold ensemble, every patient contributes one probability change. Histograms summarize these within-seed changes and are then equally averaged across seeds; probabilities are not averaged across seeds before constructing a change distribution. Panels separate models and outcome classes. Repeated seed predictions are correlated observations of the same 175 patients and do not triple the sample size. Score changes do not establish individual treatment effects}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.15}{\ignorespaces Exploratory subgroup discrimination using seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Within each seed, five fold probabilities are averaged per patient before computing AUROC; Macro averages T0--T2 AUROCs. Model entries are means $\pm $ sample SD across the three seed metrics. Paired patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean ForecastAttention minus NoJEPA difference condition on all fitted models and keep the seed set fixed. Age 50 is an exploratory reporting cutpoint. Namespace groups are parts of one clinical release, not external cohorts.}}{25}{table.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:subgroups}{{B.15}{25}{Exploratory subgroup discrimination using seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Within each seed, five fold probabilities are averaged per patient before computing AUROC; Macro averages T0--T2 AUROCs. Model entries are means $\pm $ sample SD across the three seed metrics. Paired patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean ForecastAttention minus NoJEPA difference condition on all fitted models and keep the seed set fixed. Age 50 is an exploratory reporting cutpoint. Namespace groups are parts of one clinical release, not external cohorts}{table.15}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.16}{\ignorespaces Archived epoch 20 fixed-training-probe diagnostics for seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Each entry is the mean $\pm $ sample SD of three seed-specific five-fold mean skills, distinct from probability ensembling for pCR. Skill is $1-\mathrm  {L1}_{forecast}/\mathrm  {L1}_{copy}$ within each snapshot\textquotesingle s EMA coordinates; positive is better than holding the landmark state constant. Forecast targets require a continuous actually observed visit chain. These are training-probe summaries, not best-checkpoint holdout forecast evaluations. NoJEPA has no trained-world diagnostic.}}{25}{table.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:worldprobe}{{B.16}{25}{Archived epoch 20 fixed-training-probe diagnostics for seeds 44, 2026, and 3407. Each entry is the mean $\pm $ sample SD of three seed-specific five-fold mean skills, distinct from probability ensembling for pCR. Skill is $1-\mathrm {L1}_{forecast}/\mathrm {L1}_{copy}$ within each snapshot\textquotesingle s EMA coordinates; positive is better than holding the landmark state constant. Forecast targets require a continuous actually observed visit chain. These are training-probe summaries, not best-checkpoint holdout forecast evaluations. NoJEPA has no trained-world diagnostic}{table.16}{}}
